Implements Issue #60 as a reusable Python SSR interface/application layer over accepted native RA3C 404/200 replay: eight scoped stage categories, eleven synthetic tasks, filters, details, read-only review and native source drill-down. No real approval, identity, database, model, website, customer or share access.\n\nOwner approved the sole infrastructure exception in [comment 6825546180](https://github.com/gloweaseco-leo/VRAE/pull/61#issuecomment-6825546180). Exactly one COPY line was added to infra/ra1a/Dockerfile. No isolation, privileges, dependency, collection, assertion or Guard changes.\n\nCurrent functional HEAD: `45dae1d45c5b670556afb1ef945b1349518a0ab2`. Ordinary merge: `47099b257e520caee65e28989cbec39c4b878135`, ordered parents `f54c0882c24e0e44168cce3a67d63b45ae08776a` and accepted main `225ded57add21680171cfaecac9f89df6b1af155`. All accepted main blobs/modes retained except the exact authorized Dockerfile line; PR58 reviewing and frozen QA remain unchanged. UI continues to consume native RA3C read DTO, with no reviewing/auth API integration.\n\nValidation in progress: 58 new app boundary tests passed on Python 3.11/3.13; source-bound three-size Chromium 75/75 passed, including actual filtering controls and source click-through. New-main application/P1/browser checks, full local regressions/historical replay and four fresh hosted CI receipts are being finalized. Earlier three-green/HTTP-import failures are retained, not reported as final passes.\n\nFinal exact delivery SHA and full evidence will replace this progress description. Keep Draft; no self-merge or deployment.","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-11-12T13:21:16Z","updated_at":"2026-11-12T14:05:40Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"8fa75a58f7165b09cca850fab7a85c6789e3172f","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"gloweaseco-leo:codex2/ra4c0-operator-console-shell","ref":"codex2/ra4c0-o